WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.634
Today, the National People's

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.136
Congress, the new Chinese

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.672
foreign minister, came out swinging

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.975
if the United States

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.176
does not hit the brake,

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:10.977
but continue

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.179
to speed down the wrong path.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.681
No amount of guardrails

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.616
can prevent derailing.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.585
And there will surely be conflict

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.920
and confrontation

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.022
Well, that was Ching

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.490
Jiang speaking earlier

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.357
these sharp

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.592
warnings, the latest sign

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:25.959
of how

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.360
low relations have sunk

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.763
between the United States and China.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.797
So tonight we ask,

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.699
how close are we to all out

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.567
conflict between the world's

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.636
two largest superpowers?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.072
Mark Stewart back with us this hour.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.341
He's in Tokyo on assignment.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.010
And Kylie Atwood is at the US

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.311
State Department.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.212
Mark, let's start with you.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.881
The key issues.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.548
What are they

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.016
that the foreign minister was

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:50.717
speaking about

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.120
Well, the foreign minister

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.221
really has been touching

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.123
about a lot of issues.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.458
First of all, he mentioned

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.293
even the recent balloon

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.295
shoot down in the United States.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.097
He talked about the U.S.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.398
involvement

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.101
with Taiwan and its support for Taiwan.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.203
He also accused the US of trying

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.873
to orchestrate a NATO's style alliance

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.242
in Asia and made suggestions

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.644
that Asia could be

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:20.647
the backdrop of a conflict very similar

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.549
to that of Ukraine.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.984
Certainly a long list of grievances,

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:25.952
if you will,

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:29.155
but not necessarily unexpected.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.857
And Gong at one point

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.193
was the Chinese diplomat

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.696
to the United Nations and to the US, and

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.766
has basically made this shift

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.935
from someone who has been careful

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.969
and thoughtful

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:46.005
to taking on more aggressive tones

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.875
like that of Beijing. Strong wording,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.712
very stringent wording

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.514
and a very tense tone.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.283
He is trying to establish himself as now

00:01:57.317 --> 00:02:00.653
a key player, very Beijing centric.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.590
And at the same time, as you mentioned,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.125
we have the National People's

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.426
Congress, beginning

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.928
with Xi Jinping beginning a new term.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.563
So they, too, also

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.398
want to have a very strong tone.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.100
Look, there is certainly tension

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:14.868
in this area.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.337
We have seen militaries across the region

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.638
really beef up

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.874
and include Japan, where I am now.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.609
But for the moment,

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.544
the war of words

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.846
seems to be the dominant weapon,

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.349
at least at this point, Becky.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:31.551
For I let you go.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.453
It's a war of words.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.788
We've been hearing one side of this

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.058
very loudly from the US who are bent on

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:40.827
putting into place stronger

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.830
economic measures against Beijing.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.932
We are seeing

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.234
that return by Beijing at this point.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.469
What do they put on the table

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.305
Well, it's interesting

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.139
because as you know,

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:53.640
the Chinese

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.441
economy has really been suffering,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.843
especially because of zero

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.111
COVID lockdown.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.147
The testing and the quarantines

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.916
all had a big financial toll,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.484
especially on local governments.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.518
So in a way,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.687
Beijing needs help from the West,

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.122
including the United States.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.123
However, in

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.091
just the last few hours, we heard Xi

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.359
Jinping make comments

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.294
saying that the West

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.261
and the US

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.529
have really held back

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.565
China's growth and development

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.133
and has made overtures

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.169
to heads of Chinese companies to be side

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.804
by side, step by step

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.873
with the Chinese communist government.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.242
But at the end of the day,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.644
China does need help from the outside,

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.846
and that's the United States and the West

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:36.816
Fascinating.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.952
All right, Mark, stand by, Kylie.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.220
Any response at

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.588
this point from the US side?

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.489
No, not yet.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.457
We're still waiting.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.058
State Department

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.726
has a briefing later today.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.228
But I do think that the context

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:48.962
is important here.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:49.495
Obviously,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.730
these comments made

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.799
during the National People's Congress.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.300
As Mark was saying there.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.202
And so therefore, you have a foreign

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.770
minister who's new to the job,

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.406
who is likely, you know, making comments

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.175
that make him seem, you know,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:05.311
a really tough incoming leader.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.946
In this role.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.549
And US officials will have to just wait

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.850
and see what

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.784
that looks like

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.220
in terms of his actual engagements

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.654
with U.S.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.021
officials.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:15.421
It's worth

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.356
noting that

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:17.991
he and the secretary of state

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.759
were both in India

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.527
for the foreign ministers

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.096
meetings of the G-20

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.530
just in recent weeks.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.232
And they didn't have a meeting.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.300
Now, obviously,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.268
the secretary of state

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:31.304
did have a meeting with the other top

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.473
diplomat, Wang Yi of China,

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.641
just a few weeks ago.

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.242
But that was a contentious meeting

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.611
because that was around the time,

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.414
of course, of that Chinese spy balloon.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.249
It was after the US shot that down,

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.751
which is obviously

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.052
creating a lot of tension

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.053
between the two countries.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.354
And then, of course,

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.089
accelerating those tensions.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.624
Are the warnings

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.859
from the Biden administration

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.294
that China is considering

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.562
lethal assistance to Russia

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.531
to be used in the war in Ukraine.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.633
So we've got a number of issues

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.635
that are really challenging

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:03.469
the two countries

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.804
relationship right now

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.440
and it looks a lot different than it did

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.641
at the outlook

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.842
at the beginning of this year

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.744
when it looks like U.S.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:14.047
officials and Beijing officials

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:14.981
were potentially going

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.416
to try and kind of engage

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:17.050
with one another.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.218
Well, now that has been halted.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.486
And I asked yesterday

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.054
the State Department

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:21.654
spokesperson

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.189
if there was any plans

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.324
for the secretary of state

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:26.059
to go ahead

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.061
with his rescheduled trip to Beijing

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:29.195
that was canceled

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.697
because of that balloon.

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.265
And they really had no good answer.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:32.732
There's

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.434
clearly not a date on the calendar

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.868
for that trip right now.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.870
And one thing that Ned Price said

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.405
was that the United States wishes

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:40.606
that they had more

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:41.441
and in some ways

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:44.010
deeper lines of communication with the

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:44.811
Chinese right now,

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.682
That's interesting.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.985
Let's just hear some more from what

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.821
the new foreign minister had to say.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:58.024
This is on Sino-Russian

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.959
relations

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.562
commercial.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.664
When Russia and China work together,

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:05.531
there is an impetus

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.567
for the multi polarization of the world

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.369
and the democratization

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.237
of international relations.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:11.671
And a

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.906
global strategic balance and stability

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.708
will be more guaranteed.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.610
The more turbulent the world is,

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.345
the more Sino-Russian relations

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:22.181
must move steadily forward.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:22.648
And colleague,

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.418
you alluded to the allegations,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.353
the frustration that Beijing has

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.789
with these allegations from the US about

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:31.924
that.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.026
There's no evidence for this as of yet,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.295
but the sense that China may be

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.663
getting set to send

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:40.166
lethal weapons to Russia

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:42.835
How is the US preparing

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:46.439
for the potential further

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:49.375
alignment of two of its strongest

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:50.576
adversaries at this point?

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:52.979
Yeah, it's a great

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.314
question and really what we've seen them

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.183
try and do

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.719
is get other countries on the side

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.822
of the United States in opposition

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:05.658
to this possible move by China.

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:07.460
We've seen the Secretary of State

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.363
talk to a lot of European allies

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:11.464
to make sure

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.232
that they too would oppose

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.467
that lethal assistance.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:15.835
We've actually heard

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:16.702
in recent weeks

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.838
from some of those European leaders

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.840
mirroring what the Biden administration,

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:22.875
German Chancellor Schultz

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.277
saying just last week

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.077
that they have warned

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.979
the Chinese against going ahead

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:29.582
with this lethal assistance to Ukraine.

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:30.917
So while the Biden administration

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:33.052
has repeatedly said that they don't think

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:35.388
that we are entering a period that would

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.590
mirror a new Cold War,

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.358
because the US and Chinese

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.160
economies are so integrated,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.462
which was not the case

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:43.362
with the US

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:45.765
and Russia during the Cold War.

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:48.634
It is a moment where it seems

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:49.535
that there is a big

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:51.671
polarization happening,

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:54.106
which is just the result of

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.042
many forces at play.

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:57.743
But the Ukraine war

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:00.279
appears to be accelerating

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:03.483
that bipolar nature of U.S.

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:04.617
and China competition.

